// ProjectDeliveryS453 — Sprint 453: eliciting a need records the stakeholder's words FIRST, and the elicitation procedure becomes a catalogued transferable process (issue245, D0216). EXECUTE. 2 pts.
package ProjectDeliveryS453 {
    private import EngineElement::*;
    private import EngineWork::*;
    private import EngineVerification::*;
    private import EngineRelationships::*;

    #CharteredBy dependency from elicitationThroughIntakeStory to d0216;

    part elicitationThroughIntakeStory : Story {
        :>> id = "8c3d8204-e32a-4915-b7b9-0f933a7ce5db";
        :>> title = "Sprint 453: the skill that pulls out needs is finally on the map (2 pts)";
        :>> createdAt = "2026-08-24"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> kind = WorkKind::code; :>> priority = WorkPriority::p0; :>> owner = "claudeFable5"; :>> estimatedPoints = 2;
    }

    action def DeliveryRunS453 {
        action storyElicitationThroughIntake;
        verification storyElicitationThroughIntakeDoD : Test { :>> id = "3ac2d167-58a6-4a41-9b0b-2643e10a8eae"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "DELIVERED: dcElicitationThroughIntake (resolves issue245, MEDIUM - and it is the direct answer to the human's question about pulling LATENT needs out of an average user). THE TWO FINDINGS, converged on by three of the nine panel lenses. FIRST, the capability already EXISTED and is in heavy use: the business-architecture skill runs a design/scoping dialogue deploying the Business workflow and has authored 11 Briefs, 15 Personas, 69 UseCases and 75 Needs - so the new interview process my own brief proposed would have been a FOURTH overlapping surface, which is exactly the proliferation the panel's reducer warned the whole slate against. SECOND, the real defect: that skill deployed WORKFLOWS and named no PROCESS, and the process-skill correspondence keys on a skill purpose naming .engine/processes/<name>.sysml - so keel's actual elicitation surface appeared in NO catalogue (not process list, not activation, not hardening), was enforceable by nothing, transferable by nothing, and no control noticed in either direction. Compounding it, the skill authored Needs straight out of conversations whose utterances were never recorded, which is both the mechanical cause of the unsourced population and the D0157 defect precisely: a Need with no cited utterance cannot be checked against what the stakeholder actually said, so nobody can distinguish a real demand from one written WIDER THAN THE DEMAND. WHAT WAS BUILT: .engine/processes/business-elicitation.sysml, the elicitation PROCEDURE as a first-class Process with six ordered steps - name whose needs these are; ask about PAIN not features (never offer a menu, because a chosen option is evidence about the menu and not about the need); record each answer VERBATIM as a Statement BEFORE interpreting it; translate to UserStories through the SAME intake triage vocabulary rather than a parallel scheme; author Needs that CITE their evidence by #DerivedFrom; and read the set back asking specifically what is WIDER than they meant, never whether it is good, because the second question invites assent. The business-architecture registry purpose now names the process, and the skill body puts recording-their-words at STEP 0 of Phase 1, ahead of Brief and Needs, with the rule that a Need lacking a #DerivedFrom edge must SAY it is my judgment rather than be dressed as elicited. Declared checkable = false in process-enforcement.toml with the reasoning stated, following the [intake] precedent. VERIFIED: process-skill scans 24 and passes (was 23); keel process list reports 24 declared; keel process show business-elicitation resolves; export writes definition + deploying skill + unit.toml, which works ONLY because issue241's catalogue fix landed earlier in this same run; claude-surface-drift caught the stale .claude mirror of the edited skill and sync-claude regenerated it (37/37); validate 504 + all 49 guards + check-engine + rules green. NOT CLAIMED: no guard enforces the Statement-before-Need ordering, and the declaration says why; the 599-item unsourced backlog is untouched, because back-filling Statements for conversations nobody recorded would be fabrication."; }
        part storyElicitationThroughIntakeDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "cd577277-0a17-412c-8342-c33c06511c7d"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "00417f16318529a5d0ac04ede8df3293cd9658cd"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-24"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
    }

    verification elicitationThroughIntakeRefineGate : Test { :>> id = "dd9ffcf5-5419-492b-8542-465db9b94c8a"; :>> title = "Sprint 453 refine gate (DoR)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-08-24"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "DoR. Resolves issue245 (MEDIUM), the last of the eight panel findings and the one answering the human's stated priority. Scope: give the existing elicitation procedure a process definition so it is catalogued and transferable, and wire its dialogue through the Statement chain. Explicitly NOT in scope: a new interview surface, and back-filling the unsourced backlog. 2 points."; }
    part elicitationThroughIntakeRefineGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "0cd35763-06fc-4cf6-a816-1a2a4565198a"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "00417f16318529a5d0ac04ede8df3293cd9658cd"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-24"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
    verification elicitationThroughIntakeStandupGate : Test { :>> id = "f09e551d-789b-4575-be9d-75744ef93ec9"; :>> title = "Sprint 453 standup gate"; :>> createdAt = "2026-08-24"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Approach: WIRE what exists rather than add a surface - intake (D0166) is reactive and records volunteered direction, this is active and asks, and they share one substrate on purpose so an elicited need and a volunteered one are the same kind of fact counted by one view. Statement-BEFORE-Need is the load-bearing ordering: after the Need is authored the justifying wording is gone and every later reader compares my paraphrase to my conclusion. A new process definition is keystone-locked, so D0216 co-commits. No blockers."; }
    part elicitationThroughIntakeStandupGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "e516bbf7-dd87-4045-b48d-17a4f98fc58b"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "00417f16318529a5d0ac04ede8df3293cd9658cd"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-24"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
    verification elicitationThroughIntakeImplementGate : Test { :>> id = "5ce3b0e0-dce0-492f-be07-9026b03eba3d"; :>> title = "Sprint 453 implement gate"; :>> createdAt = "2026-08-24"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "Verified by running the freshness-checked binary: process-skill 24 scanned / 0 violations (was 23); process list reports '24 declared; 11 assert guards and are switchable, 13 assert none'; process show business-elicitation resolves and names its deploying skill; process export writes processes/business-elicitation.sysml + skills/business-architecture/SKILL.md + unit.toml. claude-surface-drift FAILED on the stale .claude mirror after the skill edit and sync-claude fixed it (37/37 skills). validate 504 + all 49 guards + check-engine + rules green. Test side-effects (a minted unit id, an installed-units file) reverted before commit."; }
    part elicitationThroughIntakeImplementGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "34356bbe-96db-48d5-b2cf-39f262232f50"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "00417f16318529a5d0ac04ede8df3293cd9658cd"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-24"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
    verification elicitationThroughIntakeReviewGate : Test { :>> id = "ad6a6f64-3ae4-4554-b6a0-1fa6218bb22d"; :>> title = "Sprint 453 review gate — three passes per D0172"; :>> createdAt = "2026-08-24"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "PASS 1, CLAIMS: the guard counts, the catalogue header, the export file list and the sync output are quoted read-backs. PASS 2, BOUNDARY: (i) NO guard enforces the ordering and the enforcement contract says why - what matters is what gets asked and whether the answer was recorded before it was interpreted, neither of which a text predicate can read, and an elicitation that produced no Statement at all is indistinguishable from a conversation that never happened; (ii) the unsourced backlog is untouched by design, since fabricating Statements for unrecorded conversations is the one thing worse than the gap; (iii) the process is declared but its ADOPTION is not forced - it asserts no guard, so a project takes it deliberately, which is the honest position for a procedure whose value is judgment. PASS 3, OWN DIFF: my own brief proposed a new guided-interview process, and the panel showed that would have been the fourth overlapping elicitation surface in a repo whose complaint is too many surfaces - the correction came from three independent lenses reading the repo rather than from me, and the delivered change is strictly smaller than what I proposed. WHAT A REVIEWER SHOULD ATTACK: whether a process nobody is required to adopt, enforcing nothing, changes behaviour at all - the honest answer is that it changes MY behaviour because the skill body is what I read, and it changes an adopting project's options because the procedure is now visible and movable; neither is the same as enforcement."; }
    part elicitationThroughIntakeReviewGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "6fa7ed0a-8faa-49e0-852f-1561b2a81d1f"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "00417f16318529a5d0ac04ede8df3293cd9658cd"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-24"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
    verification elicitationThroughIntakeCloseOutGate : Test { :>> id = "f77ae1b1-a6e7-4cc1-a9f7-f5cd80dbf913"; :>> title = "Sprint 453 closeOut gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-08-24"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Autonomous closeOut (D0049). issue245 resolved; all EIGHT panel findings plus issue247 are now closed. The elicitation procedure is catalogued, exportable whole, and its dialogue records words before conclusions. validate + all 49 guards + check-engine + rules green."; }
    part elicitationThroughIntakeCloseOutGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "6ced7561-e000-4d9f-b301-84faabe553f4"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "00417f16318529a5d0ac04ede8df3293cd9658cd"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-24"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
    verification elicitationThroughIntakeRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "7beb745b-7b85-4db4-b31f-a006f845f3ed"; :>> title = "Sprint 453 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-08-24"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "Autonomous retro (D0049). AVOIDABLE-ISSUE SCAN under rcRecurrence: (1) the doc-surface mirror drifted the moment I edited a skill, and claude-surface-drift caught it immediately - a control working exactly as intended, and worth noting as the counter-example to this session's several unread-warning findings: this one was a hard failure, so it could not be skated past. (2) No new recurrence class this sprint. WELL: the panel's most useful service across the whole slate was subtractive - it deleted my proposed new interview process and replaced it with a wiring change one third the size, and it found that the surface answering the human's own stated priority was invisible to every catalogue in the engine. The compounding is also worth recording: this sprint's export verification only passes because sprint446 fixed the catalogue earlier in the same run, so the eight findings were genuinely interlocking rather than eight independent bugs. Estimate 2 pts, delivered 2."; }
    part elicitationThroughIntakeRetroGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "41e4c705-7de9-425a-9350-65cec87c3a64"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "00417f16318529a5d0ac04ede8df3293cd9658cd"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-24"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
}
